   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Unexpected cause",
     "texto": [
      "To explain something bad or unexpected that happened because of a cause, use **-는 바람에** (because of, due to): 자다 → **자는 바람에** (because I fell asleep), 오다 → **오는 바람에** (because (he/she) came). With adjectives, **-(으)ㄴ 바람에** is used.",
      "늦잠을 **자는 바람에** 지각했어요 = because I overslept, I arrived late."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Difference with -아/어서",
     "texto": [
      "**-아/어서** is a normal cause. **-는 바람에** is a cause that brings a bad or surprising result.",
      "비가 오**는 바람에** 소풍을 못 갔어요 = because of the rain I could not go on the outing."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
